//@version=6
// ===========================================================================
//  ZONE SNIPER 3.2  —  SYSTEM A  —  liquidity level + SuperTrend
//
//  Chart rules, and nothing is drawn that is not one of these:
//     the SuperTrend band            the exit, and the only job it does well
//     ONE live level                 the one you are waiting for, not a museum
//     BUY / SELL at the fill
//     the LIVE POSITION BOX          entry, stop, R ladder, running P&L in
//                                    points and in GBP at your lot size
//     a finished-trade box           entry bar to exit bar, with the result
//     one profit box in the corner
//  Everything else - ATR, entry price, stop distance, SuperTrend state - is in
//  the status line. Hover the indicator name.
//
//  WHAT THIS SYSTEM IS, and E-130 forced the wording
//  -------------------------------------------------
//  It is NOT a "liquidity sweep reversal" system. The one rule the whole
//  ICT/SMC field agrees on - wait for the candle to CLOSE back inside the level
//  - was tested on this exact data and took the result from +97.1 points to
//  +3.7, and did not separate winners from losers (MFE/MAE 0.92 -> 0.90).
//  Osler (2003, 2005), working from a real bank order book, finds price
//  ACCELERATES through stop clusters rather than reversing at them.
//
//     the LEVEL      gives a price extreme to transact at  ->  a better fill
//     the SUPERTREND gives the direction, and then the exit
//     the TRAIL      decides what the trade is worth
//
//  BOTH HALVES ARE ABLATION-MEASURED. Not decomposed - ablated: run the system
//  with the part, run it without, take the difference.
//     the LEVEL      limit inside the zone 97.1 pts / market entry 9.5 pts
//                    -> the level is worth +87.7        (E-131, 981 trades)
//     the SUPERTREND direction filter ON 97.1 / OFF 48.4
//                    -> the filter is worth +48.7       (E-127)
//  Neither is redundant. The panel on this chart re-runs the first one LIVE.
//
//  VALIDATION (E-119..E-131, 157,051 real M1 bars from 18,816,940 bid/ask
//  ticks, each bar charged its OWN measured spread):
//     the SAME zones, time-shifted  -1099.3 points -> EDGE 79.2 control se
//     out-of-sample 50.3 vs in-sample 46.7           OOS EXCEEDS IS
//     walk-forward 15.8 / 18.7 / 21.1 / 20.3 / 21.2  five of five positive
//     long +56.3, short +40.8                        both directions
//     parameters a PLATEAU, not a peak: nine of nine neighbours positive
//
//  THE TWO THINGS THAT WILL BREAK IT, stated because they are the risk:
//   1. EXIT SLIPPAGE. The exit is a stop, so it fills at or below its level.
//      0.00 -> 97.1 pts | 0.02 -> 77.5 | 0.05 -> 48.1 | 0.10 -> -1.0.
//      BREAKEVEN AT 0.10 POINTS.
//   2. SPREAD. Every number above is quoted at spread/ATR 0.11, which on M1 at
//      today's volatility is a 0.20-point spread (E-132). At 0.30 that is 0.165
//      and at 0.40 it is 0.220, so read the cost row that matches your broker:
//      0.11 -> 97.1 | 0.17 -> 82.6 | 0.25 -> 63.1 | 0.40 -> 26.7.
//
//  UNPROVEN in the vocabulary of EXPERIMENTS.md. 2018 H1 only. Never forward
//  tested. A backtest is evidence, never proof.
//
//  TESTED AND REMOVED - do not ask for these back without reading the number:
//     the SuperTrend FLIP as a signal    +0.0021R at ZERO cost, 1.2 se
//     the DEMA gate                      -3.1 control se, worse than random
//     a fixed take profit                -29.3 pts at 2R, -43.6 at 3R
//     close-back-inside confirmation     97.1 -> 3.7 points (E-130)
//     PING PONG, buy an edge target the  16.6% win rate on M1, 17.3% on M5.
//     other                              The ranges break. (E-132)
//     a chop / trend / sideways filter   filtering only removed trades
//     killzones and sessions             our feed misses 00:00 UTC daily
//     anything volume-based              both volume columns are zero
//
//  ONE THING ABOUT THE HISTORY BOXES: TradingView caps drawing objects, so on
//  a long M1 history only the most recent few hundred trades keep their box.
//  The profit box counts EVERY trade regardless - the counters are variables,
//  not drawings. If the boxes stop and the numbers keep climbing, that is the
//  cap, not a bug.
//
//  RUN IT ON XAUUSD M1.
// ===========================================================================
indicator("ZONE SNIPER 3.2", overlay = true, max_labels_count = 500,
     max_lines_count  = 500, max_boxes_count = 500, max_bars_back = 1000)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- inputs ---
gZ = "1 · THE LEVEL"
pvLen    = input.int(5,    "Swing needs this many bars either side", group = gZ, minval = 1)
useStDir = input.bool(true,"Only take levels the SuperTrend agrees with", group = gZ,
     tooltip = "E-127. Worth +48.7 points. Switch it off and the panel will show you: 48.4 instead of 97.1.")

gE = "2 · ENTRY / RISK"
pastAtr = input.float(0.50, "Limit sits this far PAST the level (ATR)", group = gE, step = 0.05)
stopAtr = input.float(4.0,  "Initial stop (ATR)",                      group = gE, step = 0.5)
waitBar = input.int(60,     "Cancel an unfilled limit after N bars",   group = gE)
maxHold = input.int(240,    "Time exit (bars)",                        group = gE)
tpR     = input.float(0.0,  "Hard take profit (R). 0 = none",          group = gE, step = 0.5,
     tooltip = "SHIPS AT 0 ON PURPOSE. A fixed target measured -29.3 points at 2R and -43.6 at 3R on this exact data (E-122). It is an input so you can watch the panel prove it, not because it is a good idea.")

gT = "3 · THE TRAIL   (the SuperTrend's only job)"
stLen  = input.int(7,     "SuperTrend ATR length", group = gT)
stMult = input.float(1.2, "SuperTrend multiplier", group = gT, step = 0.1)

gM = "4 · MONEY"
lots     = input.float(0.01, "Lots", group = gM, step = 0.01, minval = 0.01)
gbpPoint = input.float(0.787,"Account currency per point at 0.01 lots", group = gM, step = 0.001,
     tooltip = "E-081: 0.01 lots on XAUUSD is about GBP 0.787 per point and cannot go lower. This is why the TIMEFRAME sets the risk, not the account size.")
ccy      = input.string("£", "Currency symbol", group = gM)

gD = "5 · CHART"
cBuy   = input.color(#00B0FF, "Buy",  group = gD, inline = "c1")
cSell  = input.color(#FF3B5C, "Sell", group = gD, inline = "c1")
cTrail = input.color(#C9A227, "Trail",group = gD, inline = "c1")
showLevels = input.bool(true, "Live level",     group = gD, inline = "s1")
showLive   = input.bool(true, "Position box",   group = gD, inline = "s1")
showR      = input.bool(true, "R ladder",       group = gD, inline = "s1")
showHist   = input.bool(true, "Finished trades",group = gD, inline = "s2")
showPanel  = input.bool(true, "Profit box",     group = gD, inline = "s2")
panelPos   = input.string("Bottom right", "Profit box position", group = gD,
     options = ["Bottom right", "Top right", "Bottom left"])

// Pine's str.tostring format has no "+x;-x" subpattern, so the sign is explicit.
f_num(x, d) =>
    (x >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(x, d)
// points -> account currency at the chosen lot size
f_ccy(v) =>
    (v >= 0 ? "+" : "-") + ccy + str.tostring(math.abs(v) * gbpPoint * lots / 0.01, "0.00")

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ maths --
atr = ta.atr(14)
[stLine, stDir] = ta.supertrend(stMult, stLen)
bull = stDir == -1

// A pivot is only KNOWN pvLen bars after it happens. ta.pivothigh returns at
// the confirmation bar and refers to the bar pvLen back, so the level is real
// at the bar we act on. Drawing the line back to its own bar is history, not
// lookahead.
ph = ta.pivothigh(high, pvLen, pvLen)
pl = ta.pivotlow(low,  pvLen, pvLen)

// ------------------------------------------------------------- level state --
var float armBuy   = na
var float armSell  = na
var int   armBuyB  = na
var int   armSellB = na
var float armBuyPx = na
var float armSellPx= na
var line  lnBuy    = na
var line  lnSell   = na

// --------------------------------------------------------- position state ---
var int   posDir   = 0
var float posEntry = na
var float posStop  = na
var float posInit  = na      // the stop we opened with - the R unit
var float posTp    = na
var int   posBar   = na
var float posArmPx = na

// ---- THE SHADOW BOOK -------------------------------------------------------
// Identical signals, identical stop, identical trail, identical ceiling. The
// ONLY difference is that it buys at the market the moment the level is
// confirmed instead of resting a limit inside the zone. The gap between the two
// books is what the level is worth, and unlike a price-axis decomposition it
// cannot come out mechanically positive - E-131 is the whole reason this is
// here instead of a "LEVEL / TREND" split.
var int   shDir   = 0
var float shEntry = na
var float shStop  = na
var int   shBar   = na

// ------------------------------------------------------------ book-keeping --
var int   nTrades = 0
var int   nWins   = 0
var float sumPts  = 0.0
var float sumFill = 0.0
var float shPts   = 0.0
var int   shN     = 0
var float bestPts = 0.0
var float worstPts= 0.0
var float peakEq  = 0.0
var float maxDD   = 0.0
var int   firstT  = 0
var int   nLong   = 0
var int   nShort  = 0
var float ptsLong = 0.0
var float ptsShort= 0.0

dirOkBuy  = not useStDir or bull
dirOkSell = not useStDir or not bull

rawLow  = not na(pl) and dirOkBuy
rawHigh = not na(ph) and dirOkSell
newLow  = rawLow  and posDir == 0
newHigh = rawHigh and posDir == 0

// The shadow arms off the RAW signal, not off newLow/newHigh - those carry
// "posDir == 0", so gating the shadow on them would let the real book's busy
// periods decide which signals the shadow is allowed to see. E-131 ran the two
// books independently and so does this.
if (rawLow or rawHigh) and shDir == 0
    shDir   := rawLow ? 1 : -1
    shEntry := close
    shStop  := rawLow ? close - stopAtr * atr : close + stopAtr * atr
    shBar   := bar_index

if newLow
    armBuy   := pl - pastAtr * atr
    armBuyB  := bar_index
    armBuyPx := close
    if showLevels
        if not na(lnBuy)
            line.delete(lnBuy)
        lnBuy := line.new(bar_index - pvLen, pl, bar_index, pl,
             color = color.new(cBuy, 30), width = 1, extend = extend.right)

if newHigh
    armSell   := ph + pastAtr * atr
    armSellB  := bar_index
    armSellPx := close
    if showLevels
        if not na(lnSell)
            line.delete(lnSell)
        lnSell := line.new(bar_index - pvLen, ph, bar_index, ph,
             color = color.new(cSell, 30), width = 1, extend = extend.right)

// ---- a limit that never filled is not a signal. Take it off the chart. -----
if not na(armBuyB) and bar_index - armBuyB > waitBar
    armBuy  := na
    armBuyB := na
    if not na(lnBuy)
        line.delete(lnBuy)
        lnBuy := na
if not na(armSellB) and bar_index - armSellB > waitBar
    armSell  := na
    armSellB := na
    if not na(lnSell)
        line.delete(lnSell)
        lnSell := na

// ============================ THE LIVE POSITION BOX ========================
// One set of drawing objects, created on the fill and moved every bar, deleted
// on the exit. Creating a fresh set per bar is what fills a chart's 500-object
// budget in an afternoon and makes it stutter.
var box   pBox   = na
var line  pEntry = na
var line  pStop  = na
var line  pR1    = na
var line  pR2    = na
var line  pR3    = na
var label lStop  = na
var label lR1    = na
var label lR2    = na
var label lR3    = na
var label lLive  = na

// Pine takes a function's last expression as its return value, and a body made
// only of if-statements returns na. Returning an explicit bool keeps the type
// unambiguous wherever it is called.
f_killLive() =>
    if not na(pBox)
        box.delete(pBox)
    if not na(pEntry)
        line.delete(pEntry)
    if not na(pStop)
        line.delete(pStop)
    if not na(pR1)
        line.delete(pR1)
    if not na(pR2)
        line.delete(pR2)
    if not na(pR3)
        line.delete(pR3)
    if not na(lStop)
        label.delete(lStop)
    if not na(lR1)
        label.delete(lR1)
    if not na(lR2)
        label.delete(lR2)
    if not na(lR3)
        label.delete(lR3)
    if not na(lLive)
        label.delete(lLive)
    true

// ---- the fill ---------------------------------------------------------------
filledBuy  = posDir == 0 and not na(armBuy)  and low  <= armBuy  and barstate.isconfirmed
filledSell = posDir == 0 and not na(armSell) and high >= armSell and barstate.isconfirmed

if filledBuy or filledSell
    posDir   := filledBuy ? 1 : -1
    posEntry := filledBuy ? armBuy : armSell
    posStop  := posEntry - posDir * stopAtr * atr
    posInit  := posStop
    posTp    := tpR > 0 ? posEntry + posDir * tpR * math.abs(posEntry - posInit) : na
    posBar   := bar_index
    posArmPx := filledBuy ? armBuyPx : armSellPx
    armBuy   := na
    armSell  := na
    armBuyB  := na
    armSellB := na
    if not na(lnBuy)
        line.delete(lnBuy)
        lnBuy := na
    if not na(lnSell)
        line.delete(lnSell)
        lnSell := na

    if showLive
        f_killLive()
        col = posDir > 0 ? cBuy : cSell
        pBox   := box.new(posBar, posEntry, bar_index, close,
             border_color = color.new(col, 55), border_width = 1,
             bgcolor = color.new(col, 92))
        pEntry := line.new(posBar, posEntry, bar_index, posEntry,
             color = color.new(#B0BEC5, 15), width = 1, style = line.style_solid)
        pStop  := line.new(posBar, posStop, bar_index, posStop,
             color = color.new(cSell, 10), width = 1, style = line.style_dashed)
        lStop  := label.new(bar_index, posStop, "", style = label.style_label_left,
             color = color.new(chart.bg_color, 100), textcolor = color.new(cSell, 0),
             size = size.tiny)
        lLive  := label.new(bar_index, close, "", style = label.style_label_left,
             color = color.new(chart.bg_color, 100), textcolor = color.new(col, 0),
             size = size.small)
        if showR
            pR1 := line.new(posBar, posEntry, bar_index, posEntry,
                 color = color.new(cBuy, 70), width = 1, style = line.style_dotted)
            pR2 := line.new(posBar, posEntry, bar_index, posEntry,
                 color = color.new(cBuy, 70), width = 1, style = line.style_dotted)
            pR3 := line.new(posBar, posEntry, bar_index, posEntry,
                 color = color.new(cBuy, 70), width = 1, style = line.style_dotted)
            lR1 := label.new(bar_index, posEntry, "", style = label.style_label_left,
                 color = color.new(chart.bg_color, 100),
                 textcolor = color.new(cBuy, 35), size = size.tiny)
            lR2 := label.new(bar_index, posEntry, "", style = label.style_label_left,
                 color = color.new(chart.bg_color, 100),
                 textcolor = color.new(cBuy, 35), size = size.tiny)
            lR3 := label.new(bar_index, posEntry, "", style = label.style_label_left,
                 color = color.new(chart.bg_color, 100),
                 textcolor = color.new(cBuy, 35), size = size.tiny)

// ---- the shadow book's trail and exit, on the same E-110 rule as the real
// book: nothing is checked on the entry bar, or the comparison is rigged in
// favour of whichever book gets the extra bar.
if shDir != 0 and barstate.isconfirmed and bar_index > shBar
    shStop := shDir > 0 ? math.max(shStop, stLine) : math.min(shStop, stLine)
    shHit  = shDir > 0 ? low <= shStop : high >= shStop
    shOld  = bar_index - shBar >= maxHold
    if shHit or shOld
        shPts += shDir * ((shHit ? shStop : close) - shEntry)
        shN   += 1
        shDir := 0

// ---- the trail, and the exit ------------------------------------------------
// E-110: a limit filled by a bar's ADVERSE extreme must not then book that same
// bar's FAVOURABLE extreme. Six separate "validations" in this project were
// wrong because of exactly that. So nothing is checked on the entry bar.
var float exitPx = na
closedNow = false

if posDir != 0 and barstate.isconfirmed and bar_index > posBar
    // ta.supertrend returns the ACTIVE band, so one value serves both sides.
    // Ratcheted one way only: a stop that can move backwards is not a stop.
    posStop := posDir > 0 ? math.max(posStop, stLine) : math.min(posStop, stLine)
    hitStop = posDir > 0 ? low <= posStop : high >= posStop
    hitTp   = not na(posTp) and (posDir > 0 ? high >= posTp : low <= posTp)
    aged    = bar_index - posBar >= maxHold
    // a bar that touches both is scored as the LOSS. Ties lose.
    if hitStop or hitTp or aged
        exitPx    := hitStop ? posStop : hitTp ? posTp : close
        pts       = posDir * (exitPx - posEntry)
        // FILL VS SIGNAL. An entry-quality diagnostic, NOT a share of the
        // profit. E-131: splitting a trade at the arm price is exact and
        // useless - it reads +691.9 / -594.8 against a +97.1 result, and is
        // positive on 100.0% of trades because the 0.50 ATR offset makes it so
        // by construction. It measures the offset, not the level.
        pFill     = posDir * (posArmPx - posEntry)
        if nTrades == 0
            firstT := time
        nTrades  += 1
        nWins    += pts > 0 ? 1 : 0
        sumPts   += pts
        sumFill  += pFill
        bestPts  := math.max(bestPts,  pts)
        worstPts := math.min(worstPts, pts)
        peakEq   := math.max(peakEq, sumPts)
        maxDD    := math.max(maxDD, peakEq - sumPts)
        if posDir > 0
            nLong   += 1
            ptsLong += pts
        else
            nShort   += 1
            ptsShort += pts

        if showHist
            won = pts > 0
            box.new(posBar, math.max(posEntry, exitPx), bar_index, math.min(posEntry, exitPx),
                 border_color = color.new(won ? cBuy : cSell, 45), border_width = 1,
                 bgcolor = color.new(won ? cBuy : cSell, 90))
            label.new(bar_index, posDir > 0 ? math.max(posEntry, exitPx) : math.min(posEntry, exitPx),
                 f_num(pts, "0.0") + "pt  " + f_ccy(pts),
                 style = posDir > 0 ? label.style_label_lower_left : label.style_label_upper_left,
                 color = color.new(chart.bg_color, 100),
                 textcolor = color.new(won ? cBuy : cSell, 0), size = size.tiny)

        f_killLive()
        posDir   := 0
        posEntry := na
        posStop  := na
        posBar   := na
        closedNow := true

// ---- move the live objects. Once per bar, never recreated. -----------------
if posDir != 0 and showLive and not na(pBox)
    live = posDir * (close - posEntry)
    col  = live >= 0 ? cBuy : cSell
    box.set_right(pBox, bar_index)
    box.set_top(pBox, math.max(posEntry, close))
    box.set_bottom(pBox, math.min(posEntry, close))
    box.set_bgcolor(pBox, color.new(col, 92))
    box.set_border_color(pBox, color.new(col, 55))
    line.set_x2(pEntry, bar_index)
    line.set_x2(pStop, bar_index)
    line.set_y1(pStop, posStop)
    line.set_y2(pStop, posStop)
    risk = posDir * (posEntry - posStop)     // negative once the trail is above entry
    label.set_xy(lStop, bar_index, posStop)
    label.set_text(lStop, (risk > 0 ? "SL  " : "LOCKED  ") + f_num(-risk, "0.0") + "pt  "
         + f_ccy(-risk))
    label.set_textcolor(lStop, color.new(risk > 0 ? cSell : cBuy, 0))
    label.set_xy(lLive, bar_index, close)
    label.set_text(lLive, f_num(live, "0.0") + "pt   " + f_ccy(live))
    label.set_textcolor(lLive, color.new(col, 0))
    if showR and not na(pR1)
        // The R ladder is a REFERENCE, not a target. This system has no take
        // profit: E-122 measured a fixed 2R at -29.3 points and 3R at -43.6 on
        // these exact entries. The rungs are here so you can see where price is
        // in units of your own risk, and what each one is worth in money.
        r = math.abs(posEntry - posInit)
        for i = 1 to 3
            ln = i == 1 ? pR1 : i == 2 ? pR2 : pR3
            lb = i == 1 ? lR1 : i == 2 ? lR2 : lR3
            y  = posEntry + posDir * i * r
            line.set_xy1(ln, posBar, y)
            line.set_xy2(ln, bar_index, y)
            label.set_xy(lb, bar_index, y)
            reached = posDir > 0 ? high >= y : low <= y
            label.set_text(lb, (not na(posTp) and math.abs(y - posTp) < syminfo.mintick
                 ? "TP " : "") + str.tostring(i) + "R  " + f_ccy(i * r))
            label.set_textcolor(lb, color.new(posDir > 0 ? cBuy : cSell, reached ? 10 : 55))

// ---- what is on the candles, and this is the complete list -----------------
plot(stLine, "SuperTrend trail", color = color.new(cTrail, 45), linewidth = 1)

plotshape(filledBuy,  "BUY",  shape.labelup,   location.belowbar, color = cBuy,
     text = "BUY",  textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(filledSell, "SELL", shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color = cSell,
     text = "SELL", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)

plot(showLevels and posDir == 0 and not na(armBuy)  ? armBuy  : na, "Buy limit",
     color = color.new(cBuy, 25),  style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 2)
plot(showLevels and posDir == 0 and not na(armSell) ? armSell : na, "Sell limit",
     color = color.new(cSell, 25), style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 2)

// ============================== THE PROFIT BOX =============================
var table tp = na

f_row(r, a, b, c, col) =>
    table.cell(tp, 0, r, a, text_color = color.new(#8FA3B8, 0), text_size = size.small,
         text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(tp, 1, r, b, text_color = col, text_size = size.small,
         text_halign = text.align_right)
    table.cell(tp, 2, r, c, text_color = color.new(#8FA3B8, 25), text_size = size.tiny,
         text_halign = text.align_right)

f_sep(r, cap) =>
    table.cell(tp, 0, r, cap, text_color = color.new(#5C7089, 0), text_size = size.tiny,
         text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(tp, 1, r, "", text_color = color.new(#5C7089, 0))
    table.cell(tp, 2, r, "", text_color = color.new(#5C7089, 0))

if barstate.islast and showPanel
    if not na(tp)
        table.delete(tp)
    pos = panelPos == "Top right" ? position.top_right :
          panelPos == "Bottom left" ? position.bottom_left : position.bottom_right
    tp := table.new(pos, 3, 15, border_width = 1,
         bgcolor = color.new(#0E1621, 8), border_color = color.new(#2A3A4D, 40),
         frame_color = color.new(#2A3A4D, 20), frame_width = 1)

    cVal  = color.new(#E6EDF5, 0)
    cPos  = color.new(cBuy, 0)
    cNeg  = color.new(cSell, 0)
    winPc = nTrades > 0 ? 100.0 * nWins / nTrades : 0.0
    avg   = nTrades > 0 ? sumPts / nTrades : 0.0
    days  = nTrades > 0 ? math.max(1.0, (time - firstT) / 86400000.0) : 1.0

    table.cell(tp, 0, 0, "ZONE SNIPER 3.2", text_color = cVal, text_size = size.small,
         text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(tp, 1, 0, "", text_color = cVal)
    table.cell(tp, 2, 0, posDir == 0 ? "flat" : posDir > 0 ? "LONG" : "SHORT",
         text_color = posDir == 0 ? color.new(#8FA3B8, 0) : posDir > 0 ? cPos : cNeg,
         text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_right)

    // POINTS FIRST. E-074: the best per-trade gate set in this project banked
    // the LEAST money, so R and expectancy are not the unit that matters.
    f_row(1, "points",    f_num(sumPts, "0.0"), f_ccy(sumPts), sumPts >= 0 ? cPos : cNeg)
    f_row(2, "trades",    str.tostring(nTrades),
             str.tostring(nTrades / days, "0.0") + "/day", cVal)
    f_row(3, "win rate",  str.tostring(winPc, "0.0") + "%",
             str.tostring(nWins) + "W " + str.tostring(nTrades - nWins) + "L", cVal)
    f_row(4, "avg trade", f_num(avg, "0.000"), "points", avg >= 0 ? cPos : cNeg)

    // ---- WHAT EACH PART IS WORTH, measured live on your bars ----------
    // Not a decomposition - an ABLATION. The shadow book takes the same signals
    // with the same stop and the same trail and simply buys at the market
    // instead of resting a limit inside the zone. The gap is the level's
    // contribution and it is free to come out negative, which is the point.
    // E-131 on 981 real trades: limit 97.1, market 9.5, the level worth +87.7.
    // SuperTrend's half is measured the same way - switch the "Only take levels
    // the SuperTrend agrees with" input off and read this box again. Measured
    // (E-127): filter OFF 48.4, filter ON 97.1, so it is worth +48.7.
    f_sep(5, "── what each part is worth ──")
    f_row(6, "limit in zone",    f_num(sumPts, "0.0"), "shipped", sumPts >= 0 ? cPos : cNeg)
    f_row(7, "market at signal", f_num(shPts, "0.0"),
             str.tostring(shN) + " trades", shPts >= 0 ? cPos : cNeg)
    f_row(8, "the level adds",   f_num(sumPts - shPts, "0.0"), "points",
             sumPts - shPts >= 0 ? cPos : cNeg)
    f_row(9, "fill vs signal",   nTrades > 0 ? f_num(sumFill / nTrades, "0.000") : "-",
             "pts/trade", cVal)

    f_sep(10, "── risk ──")
    f_row(11, "best / worst", f_num(bestPts, "0.0") + " / " + str.tostring(worstPts, "0.0"),
              "points", cVal)
    f_row(12, "max drawdown", f_num(-maxDD, "0.0"), f_ccy(-maxDD), cNeg)
    f_row(13, "long / short", f_num(ptsLong, "0.0") + " / " + f_num(ptsShort, "0.0"),
              str.tostring(nLong) + " / " + str.tostring(nShort), cVal)
    f_row(14, "open", posDir == 0 ? "-" : f_num(posDir * (close - posEntry), "0.0"),
              posDir == 0 ? str.tostring(lots, "0.00") + " lots"
                          : f_ccy(posDir * (close - posEntry)),
              posDir == 0 ? cVal : (posDir * (close - posEntry) >= 0 ? cPos : cNeg))

// the rest goes in the status line, off the candles
plot(posDir, "Position (1 long, -1 short)",   display = display.status_line)
plot(posDir != 0 ? posEntry : na, "Entry",    display = display.status_line)
plot(posDir != 0 ? posDir * (close - posEntry) : na, "Open points",
     display = display.status_line)
plot(posDir != 0 ? math.abs(close - posStop) / atr : na, "Stop distance (ATR)",
     display = display.status_line)
plot(atr, "ATR(14)",                          display = display.status_line)
plot(bull ? 1 : -1, "SuperTrend (1 bull)",    display = display.status_line)

alertcondition(filledBuy,  "ZS BUY",   "Zone Sniper 3.2 BUY filled")
alertcondition(filledSell, "ZS SELL",  "Zone Sniper 3.2 SELL filled")
alertcondition(closedNow,  "ZS CLOSE", "Zone Sniper 3.2 trade closed")
